From e11338de119df16a782fc8a6451e3b4dd0913ca8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marius Gripsgard <marius@ubports.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 19:42:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Vendor the Application API headers instead of depending on
 lomiri-api

qtmir is the sole implementer of lomiri-shell-application, so there's
no value fetching those interface headers from a separate API package
at build time. They move into include/lomiri/shell/application/ here
(stripped of the inert LOMIRI_API/SymbolExport.h, which has never
actually done anything outside lomiri-api's own build); lomiri-api
drops its copy in a companion commit. CMakeLists.txt files that
referenced them via the old APPLICATION_API_INCLUDEDIR/_INCLUDE_DIRS
pkg-config variables now point at the local copy instead.

The lomiri-shell-application pkg-config module lomiri still consumes
is generated here too, folded into the existing libqt5mir1server-dev
package rather than a new one, since a shell consuming it already
needs to build against a Mir server implementing the interface.

(cherry picked from commit bd7f9e81adc621fc140b6367b6cc6b71e313ccb2)
